ccusage native runtime (Rust)
-----------------------------
The native ccusage binary bundled inside the platform-specific packages
(@ccusage/ccusage-<platform>-<arch>) is compiled from ccusage's own Rust
workspace (https://github.com/ccusage/ccusage/tree/main/rust), which links
119 third-party Rust crates as pinned in that workspace's rust/Cargo.lock
(fetched directly from the upstream repository for this review). A
representative sample of the most significant crates was checked against the
crates.io registry metadata:

  - MIT / Apache-2.0 (dual, standard Rust-ecosystem default): serde,
    serde_json, libc, regex-automata, rustls-pki-types, sqlite3-sys,
    zeroize, aws-lc-rs (Apache-2.0 only)
  - MIT only: mimalloc
  - MIT / Unlicense (dual): jiff, aho-corasick
  - ISC: rustls-webpki, untrusted
  - Apache-2.0 / ISC / MIT (triple, permissive): rustls
  - Apache-2.0 AND ISC (combined): ring
  - BSD-3-Clause: subtle
  - CDLA-Permissive-2.0 (a permissive, non-copyleft data license used for the
    bundled Mozilla root-certificate list): webpki-roots

No copyleft (GPL/LGPL/AGPL) licenses were found among the crates inspected.
The broader ~119-crate tree was not individually verified beyond this sample,
but is consistent with the typical permissive Rust-ecosystem mix of MIT,
Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD, and similar licenses. This summary is a due-diligence
aid, not an exhaustive SPDX bill of materials; see ccusage's own repository
(rust/Cargo.lock) for the authoritative dependency manifest.
